Found by k211. t/26, t/52, t/53, t/65 and t/66 skip their reference half unless ../../node_modules/nunjucks exists (relative to perl/t). Node resolves node_modules up the directory tree, so in a checkout nested in another (a .claude/worktrees/agent-* worktree without its own node_modules) the reference would run, yet these files skip – silently green. Done: the check asks node itself (for example `node -e "require.resolve(\"nunjucks\")"` from the repo root) or walks up as node does; a skip names the reason; one shared helper in t/lib instead of five copies.

